1
00:00:08,780 --> 00:00:10,140
No! Asuna!

2
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:11,570
Free?

3
00:00:11,840 --> 00:00:12,800
No!

4
00:00:13,220 --> 00:00:15,060
Let go of me, no!

5
00:00:18,160 --> 00:00:20,260
Asuna! Asuna!

6
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,300
Asuna!

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:24,140
Asuna! Asuna!

8
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:30,580
Run, Xenon!

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:37,630
Kirito...

10
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:41,180
What the hell?

11
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,380
Get off me!

12
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,140
Master, it's all your fault!

13
00:00:48,380 --> 00:00:49,400
She's mine!

14
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:50,900
She's mine, damn it!

15
00:00:51,480 --> 00:00:53,060
Stay away from her!

16
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:58,930
Kirito!

17
00:01:19,360 --> 00:01:20,190
Kirito!

18
00:01:20,320 --> 00:01:21,240
He got me.

19
00:01:21,840 --> 00:01:23,620
It happened so fast.

20
00:01:24,140 --> 00:01:25,637
I didn't even see the needle!

21
00:01:25,720 --> 00:01:26,550
I know!

22
00:01:26,633 --> 00:01:27,987
I'm gonna take a look, okay?

23
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:34,900
Hang on, I'm not gonna
let you die like this!

24
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:08,140
Um, hey, you got this
weird thing on your chest.

25
00:02:11,720 --> 00:02:14,757
Please tell me that's where
you hit me with the needle.

26
00:02:14,840 --> 00:02:16,700
It looks like it, I guess.

27
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:18,569
What is that thing anyway?

28
00:02:20,320 --> 00:02:24,057
It's one of the electrodes from this
heart monitor I was hooked up to.

29
00:02:24,140 --> 00:02:25,260
Heart monitor?

30
00:02:26,180 --> 00:02:27,080
Never mind.

31
00:02:27,340 --> 00:02:29,277
You know, you scared the hell out of me.

32
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,340
I scared you?

33
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:31,892
How do you think I feel?

34
00:02:32,080 --> 00:02:35,080
I thought you were gonna
die just now, you dumbass!

35
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,720
Hey, easy!

36
00:02:47,440 --> 00:02:49,840
He's not dead, is he?

37
00:02:56,260 --> 00:02:58,180
No, he's still got a pulse.

38
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:11,780
You're crazy, but thank
you for coming over.

39
00:03:12,340 --> 00:03:15,020
No, thank you for
clocking him when you did.

40
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:17,756
I'm sorry I couldn't get here sooner.

41
00:03:21,360 --> 00:03:22,560
You okay?

42
00:03:24,140 --> 00:03:26,360
I'm sorry.

43
00:03:57,300 --> 00:03:59,712
I can't wait to see the look on her face.

44
00:03:59,960 --> 00:04:00,790
I know, right?

45
00:04:03,500 --> 00:04:05,820
Next time you want to meet, be on time.

46
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:09,250
Seriously?

47
00:04:09,960 --> 00:04:12,357
Girl, you've been acting
way too cocky lately.

48
00:04:12,440 --> 00:04:13,270
She's right.

49
00:04:13,353 --> 00:04:14,946
We should teach you a lesson.

50
00:04:22,040 --> 00:04:24,957
No you guys it's cool we're
all friends here, right?

51
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:26,897
It's good to have friends.

52
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:30,497
They come in real handy,
especially when you need a loan.

53
00:04:30,580 --> 00:04:34,680
Speaking of, I need 20k, buddy!

54
00:04:44,580 --> 00:04:48,220
I told you before, I'm not
lending you guys any money.

55
00:04:49,760 --> 00:04:53,277
You'll change your mind after I
show you what my brother gave me.

56
00:04:53,360 --> 00:04:54,360
I doubt it.

57
00:05:01,900 --> 00:05:06,135
Get this, he told me not to point
this at anyone, but what does he know?

58
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:09,808
I mean, you've seen one before,
so it doesn't bug you, right?

59
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,040
Or does it, Asada?

60
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:16,874
Get on your knees and say you're sorry.

61
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:31,880
Crap, it's not working.

62
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:39,110
Ow!

63
00:05:43,700 --> 00:05:45,700
Government issue M-1911.

64
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,840
Your brother has good taste.

65
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:50,121
It's not really my style, though.

66
00:05:50,640 --> 00:05:54,287
And for future reference, it
only fires when the safety's off.

67
00:06:10,760 --> 00:06:12,040
Hey, whoa!

68
00:06:12,420 --> 00:06:13,497
Your brother's right.

69
00:06:13,580 --> 00:06:15,639
You shouldn't point this at people.

70
00:06:17,640 --> 00:06:18,470
Here.

71
00:06:20,900 --> 00:06:22,540
Oh my god, are you okay?

72
00:06:22,940 --> 00:06:23,800
Get up, Endo!

73
00:06:27,260 --> 00:06:28,440
See you around.

74
00:06:39,640 --> 00:06:42,287
They say the first step's
always the hardest.

75
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,820
Hey, Asada!

76
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,440
Do you know that guy?

77
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,240
Is he your boyfriend?

78
00:07:11,100 --> 00:07:11,930
Really?

79
00:07:12,013 --> 00:07:16,542
When I said I'd meet you, I didn't think
you'd part yourself in front of my school.

80
00:07:16,760 --> 00:07:17,677
Hmm? Oh.

81
00:07:17,760 --> 00:07:18,860
What's up, Sinon?

82
00:07:25,620 --> 00:07:29,091
Kyoji Shinkawa and his older
brother Shoichi were arrested.

83
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:33,596
During the interrogation, it came
out that another person was involved.

84
00:07:34,540 --> 00:07:38,480
This third death gun, Atsushi
Kanamoto, is still out there.

85
00:07:38,800 --> 00:07:41,565
but Kikuoka says they'll
catch him soon enough.

86
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:46,037
They got the idea of creating
the Death Gun character when

87
00:07:46,120 --> 00:07:49,767
Shoichi got the invisibility
cloak through a real money trade.

88
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,318
Using the cloak and some binoculars,

89
00:07:53,560 --> 00:07:57,442
Shoichi started stealing the
real-world info of the other players.

90
00:07:57,840 --> 00:08:02,546
Meanwhile, his little brother Kyochi was
having issues with his avatar, Spiegel.

91
00:08:04,080 --> 00:08:07,198
These players who think it's
all about their agility?

92
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:09,224
Man, they're living in a dream.

93
00:08:09,780 --> 00:08:13,074
Spiegel was an AGI type, which
Zexine used to recommend.

94
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:18,780
But Zexine shifted his stats to an
STR-VIT combo, and that pissed Kyoji off.

95
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:24,020
When Shoichi found out, he gave
Kyoji Zexine's name and address IRL.

96
00:08:24,660 --> 00:08:27,542
Then, they started talking
about how to kill him.

97
00:08:28,120 --> 00:08:30,944
They say they weren't
serious about it at first.

98
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:32,400
But day after day,

99
00:08:32,640 --> 00:08:37,228
the more they talked about it, the more
it seemed they could get away with it.

100
00:08:37,500 --> 00:08:41,617
For their plan to work, they needed
two things from their dad's hospital.

101
00:08:41,700 --> 00:08:47,060
A master key card used to open doors in
emergencies, and a lethal drug for the deed.

102
00:08:47,800 --> 00:08:50,153
They researched their victims carefully,

103
00:08:50,440 --> 00:08:55,037
narrowing the list down to the ones who
lived alone in low-security apartments.

104
00:08:55,120 --> 00:08:59,080
Using the key card, Shoichi broke
into their first victim's place,

105
00:08:59,540 --> 00:09:01,800
Shigemura, a .k .a. Zekseed.

106
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:05,987
The brothers worked out the exact
time he was supposed to die.

107
00:09:06,380 --> 00:09:09,377
when Kyoji logged in as his
brother's avatar Sterben

108
00:09:09,460 --> 00:09:12,401
and announced himself as
Death Gun and shot Zexit.

109
00:09:13,000 --> 00:09:16,800
Their second victim, Usushio
Tarako, was killed the same way.

110
00:09:18,140 --> 00:09:20,517
But instead of being scared of Death Gun,

111
00:09:20,600 --> 00:09:24,071
the other players in GGO treated
it like some kind of joke.

112
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:27,317
Shoichi and his partners were furious,

113
00:09:27,400 --> 00:09:30,477
so they decided to kill some
players during the B .O .B.

114
00:09:30,560 --> 00:09:31,390
final.

115
00:09:31,820 --> 00:09:35,660
They found three who met the same
criteria as Zexit and Tarako,

116
00:09:37,140 --> 00:09:39,600
Hailrider, Garrett, and Sinon.

117
00:09:47,520 --> 00:09:51,597
Killing three people was going to make
things hard for just the two of them, though.

118
00:09:51,680 --> 00:09:52,510
Yeah.

119
00:09:52,593 --> 00:09:54,077
To be in sync with Death Gun,

120
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:56,137
the person doing the
real-world killing had to

121
00:09:56,220 --> 00:09:58,757
make sure they'd be at each
target's house on time.

122
00:09:58,840 --> 00:10:02,997
So they recruited that Kanamoto guy you
told me about to be the third Death Gun.

123
00:10:03,080 --> 00:10:05,257
Where'd they find him, though? Simple.

124
00:10:05,340 --> 00:10:07,720
Kanamoto was an old friend of Shoichi's.

125
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:11,180
They were both part of
Laughing Coffin and SAO.

126
00:10:11,440 --> 00:10:14,157
We found out his handle
there was Johnny Black.

127
00:10:14,240 --> 00:10:15,416
That sound familiar?

128
00:10:16,260 --> 00:10:17,860
Yeah, he worked with Zaza.

129
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:20,984
I think his weapon of
choice was a poison knife.

130
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:26,679
They put Kanamoto on Pale Rider and
Garrett, because he lived nearby.

131
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:29,575
Sinon, on the other hand, was Kyoji's.

132
00:10:30,120 --> 00:10:32,717
See, Shoichi was the one
who usually did the killing.

133
00:10:32,800 --> 00:10:36,860
But for this one job, Kyoji
insisted on being the one to do it.

134
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,768
Um, is that what he wanted?

135
00:10:41,040 --> 00:10:41,870
For real?

136
00:10:41,953 --> 00:10:44,860
Did Shinka, I mean, Kyoji, say that? No.

137
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:48,417
His brother was the one who gave
us all the details of their plan.

138
00:10:48,500 --> 00:10:50,180
Kyoji still refuses to talk.

139
00:10:50,680 --> 00:10:51,800
He does, huh?

140
00:10:53,760 --> 00:10:56,457
Speaking of, we found out a
little more about Shoichi.

141
00:10:56,540 --> 00:10:59,246
Health-wise, he'd been
sickly since childhood.

142
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,595
His father pretty much gave up on him,

143
00:11:01,720 --> 00:11:05,132
so he decided early on to hand
the hospital over to Kyoji.

144
00:11:05,240 --> 00:11:06,517
Staying sharp, ma 'am.

145
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:07,659
Locked and loaded.

146
00:11:09,380 --> 00:11:12,439
Even so, the brothers seemed
to be close growing up.

147
00:11:12,740 --> 00:11:15,817
But then Shoichi got
obsessed with MMORPGs,

148
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:20,220
and in 2022, he got trapped
in Sword Art Online.

149
00:11:22,320 --> 00:11:25,737
After he got out, Shoichi
only spoke to Kyoji about it.

150
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:29,417
He bragged about how in that
world he was a real mass murderer,

151
00:11:29,500 --> 00:11:30,940
and how he was feared.

152
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:34,440
In Kyoji's eyes, his
big brother was a hero.

153
00:11:35,120 --> 00:11:36,200
As for Shoichi,

154
00:11:36,540 --> 00:11:39,777
he's sticking with the story that
everything about the Death Gun concept,

155
00:11:39,860 --> 00:11:42,417
including the murders,
was just part of a game.

156
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:45,697
That his actions here, like
gathering intel on victims,

157
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:49,457
prepping for the murders, and committing
them, were no different than an SAO.

158
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:51,840
The dark side of VR Miss.

159
00:11:52,300 --> 00:11:53,337
That's what it is.

160
00:11:53,420 --> 00:11:56,300
his reality got a lot less real.

161
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:58,180
Yeah, good point.

162
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:00,780
And how are you handling yours?

163
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:05,660
I feel like I left a
part of me back in SAO.

164
00:12:05,860 --> 00:12:09,389
So right now, there's less of
me here than there was before.

165
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:10,780
I don't know.

166
00:12:11,240 --> 00:12:12,122
You don't know?

167
00:12:12,360 --> 00:12:14,480
Do you want to go back? Seriously?

168
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:16,289
How could you ask me that?

169
00:12:17,080 --> 00:12:18,360
Um, wait a sec.

170
00:12:18,560 --> 00:12:21,417
You're kind of contradicting
what you told me the other day.

171
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:22,330
What?

172
00:12:22,413 --> 00:12:25,449
You said there's no such thing
as a virtual world, remember?

173
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:28,601
That like, wherever you
were, that's your reality.

174
00:12:28,800 --> 00:12:33,620
Where I am right now, here,
this world is my reality.

175
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:39,424
And even if you told me this was a virtual
world, it would still be reality to me.

176
00:12:39,720 --> 00:12:41,160
You see what I mean?

177
00:12:41,900 --> 00:12:42,800
I guess.

178
00:12:44,400 --> 00:12:45,520
Yeah, you're right.

179
00:12:45,900 --> 00:12:47,700
I gotta hand it to you, Sinon.

180
00:12:48,020 --> 00:12:51,577
What you said just now might be the only
good thing to come out of this nightmare.

181
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:53,260
No, put a sock in it.

182
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,020
Sorry, I'm with Kirito on this one.

183
00:12:58,620 --> 00:13:01,597
Well, I told you pretty much
all we've found out so far.

184
00:13:01,680 --> 00:13:04,300
You have any questions before I go? I do.

185
00:13:04,980 --> 00:13:08,686
Has there been any word on what's
going to happen to Kyoji yet?

186
00:13:09,960 --> 00:13:12,697
Based on his brother's
confession and their behavior,

187
00:13:12,780 --> 00:13:16,192
they'll most likely be sent
to a medical detention center.

188
00:13:16,520 --> 00:13:19,520
I doubt either one knows
what reality is anymore.

189
00:13:20,300 --> 00:13:22,320
No, I don't think that's true.

190
00:13:23,020 --> 00:13:25,537
I don't know anything
about Kyochi's brother.

191
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:26,561
I never met him.

192
00:13:26,700 --> 00:13:32,120
But I've known Kyochi a long time and, well,
I think his reality was Gungail Online.

193
00:13:32,520 --> 00:13:34,980
He'd pretty much given up on this world.

194
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:40,960
There was nothing left for him other
than GGO, so he made that his reality.

195
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:46,740
He'd spend hours in it, grinding away,
boosting his XP and trying to be the best.

196
00:13:47,460 --> 00:13:50,620
I guess the stress got
to be too much for him.

197
00:13:50,780 --> 00:13:52,000
From playing a game?

198
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:55,820
I know you can lose track
of time, but reality? Sure.

199
00:13:56,240 --> 00:14:00,640
At some point, Kyoji just swapped
out one for the other, his real life,

200
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,500
for his virtual one.

201
00:14:02,700 --> 00:14:04,460
Okay, but why?

202
00:14:04,780 --> 00:14:07,080
I don't know, but I wish I did.

203
00:14:08,740 --> 00:14:11,400
Kirito, why do you think he did it?

204
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:13,260
To get stronger.

205
00:14:14,480 --> 00:14:15,400
You're right.

206
00:14:16,020 --> 00:14:17,608
I guess I was the same way.

207
00:14:18,140 --> 00:14:22,440
When it comes down to it, maybe
all us VRMMO players are the same.

208
00:14:22,780 --> 00:14:24,604
All we want is to get stronger.

209
00:14:26,320 --> 00:14:27,150
Mr.

210
00:14:27,233 --> 00:14:30,000
Kikwoka, I'd like to go see
him if that's all right.

211
00:14:30,280 --> 00:14:33,857
There's so much I want to tell him,
like what we were just talking about.

212
00:14:33,940 --> 00:14:36,822
And other stuff I've been
thinking, if it's okay.

213
00:14:37,760 --> 00:14:39,760
You're a strong person to want to.

214
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,753
And I, for one, think it's a great idea.

215
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:46,546
He can't have visitors yet, but
when he can, I'll let you know.

216
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:49,989
Well, I have to get
back to the office now.

217
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:51,690
Okay.

218
00:14:51,773 --> 00:14:52,728
Thanks for taking the time.

219
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:55,300
Yes, thank you for talking to us.

220
00:14:55,520 --> 00:14:56,814
Don't even mention it.

221
00:14:57,020 --> 00:15:00,137
You guys risked your lives, and
God knows how many you saved.

222
00:15:00,220 --> 00:15:01,749
It's the least I could do.

223
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:04,360
Oh, by the way, Kirito,

224
00:15:05,460 --> 00:15:07,920
Death Gun, or Shoichi Shinkawa,

225
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:12,297
or Red-Eyed Zaza, or whatever you want to
call him, asked me to give you a message.

226
00:15:12,380 --> 00:15:16,086
If you don't want to hear it,
say the word and I'll tear it up.

227
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,680
I'll hear it.

228
00:15:19,980 --> 00:15:20,860
You got it.

229
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:23,090
He wrote,

230
00:15:23,540 --> 00:15:25,860
If you think this is over, it's not.

231
00:15:26,220 --> 00:15:28,537
You don't have what it takes to end this.

232
00:15:28,620 --> 00:15:30,796
Sooner or later, you'll realize that.

233
00:15:31,220 --> 00:15:32,100
It's showtime.

234
00:15:33,100 --> 00:15:33,930
That's it.

235
00:15:47,440 --> 00:15:51,060
Hey, uh, Sinon? Hmm? What's up?

236
00:15:51,800 --> 00:15:54,080
Are you free right now?

237
00:15:55,120 --> 00:15:56,473
What do you mean, free?

238
00:15:56,560 --> 00:15:57,390
Free for what?

239
00:16:05,080 --> 00:16:08,500
So, this is where you're taking me? Yep.

240
00:16:08,780 --> 00:16:11,251
There's someone inside I want you to meet.

241
00:16:12,380 --> 00:16:13,860
Well, it's about time.

242
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:18,097
It made us wait so darn long, I wouldn't
have had two slices of apple pie.

243
00:16:18,180 --> 00:16:20,017
If I get fat, it's all your fault.

244
00:16:20,100 --> 00:16:22,120
How's that my fault? Jeez.

245
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,500
Come on, Kirito.

246
00:16:25,620 --> 00:16:27,357
Are you going to introduce us or what?

247
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,380
Huh? Oh, right. Sorry.

248
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,160
This is Shino Asada, a .k .a. Sinon.

249
00:16:32,500 --> 00:16:34,618
Gun Gale Online's third super champ.

250
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:36,620
Oh, don't say that.

251
00:16:39,620 --> 00:16:42,680
These are my friends from my time in SAO.

252
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:43,857
Rika, a .k .a.

253
00:16:43,940 --> 00:16:46,120
Liz, Blacksmith and Swindler. Huh?

254
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,245
What the hell did you call me?

255
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:51,640
And that's Asuna, the berserk healer.

256
00:16:51,920 --> 00:16:53,460
Real name, Asuna Yuki.

257
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:55,350
Berserk?

258
00:16:56,420 --> 00:16:59,420
You want to grab a seat
and get something to drink?

259
00:17:01,000 --> 00:17:02,237
That's what Star...

260
00:17:02,320 --> 00:17:03,880
I mean, sterben means?

261
00:17:04,780 --> 00:17:07,320
A term hospitals use for death.

262
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:11,713
What was he thinking, giving
his avatar a name like that?

263
00:17:11,840 --> 00:17:12,777
If I were you,

264
00:17:12,860 --> 00:17:16,077
I wouldn't try to find some deeper
meaning in the name he gave his avatar.

265
00:17:16,160 --> 00:17:19,717
A lot of times it boils down to
whatever a player thinks sounds cool.

266
00:17:19,800 --> 00:17:21,280
Oh, that explains it.

267
00:17:21,400 --> 00:17:23,077
This whole time I thought
you gave your avatar

268
00:17:23,160 --> 00:17:24,977
your name because you lacked imagination.

269
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:25,890
Zip it!

270
00:17:26,300 --> 00:17:30,180
I do so have imagination. Lots
of it! Okay, geez. Whatever.

271
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:37,740
So anyway, I'm super stoked you're here.

272
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:40,957
It's always cool to meet
another girl VRMMO player.

273
00:17:41,040 --> 00:17:42,000
You said it.

274
00:17:42,320 --> 00:17:44,600
I hope we can be great friends, Asura.

275
00:17:55,940 --> 00:17:57,577
Listen, Asura. Shino.

276
00:17:57,660 --> 00:18:01,037
There's another reason for us
asking you to come here today.

277
00:18:01,120 --> 00:18:02,140
What is it?

278
00:18:03,140 --> 00:18:06,081
Sinon, I'm sorry to put
you on the spot like this.

279
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:13,180
I, uh, I told Asuna and Liz about what
happened to you when you were younger.

280
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,740
I didn't have a choice.

281
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:17,176
I needed their help.

282
00:18:18,240 --> 00:18:19,120
I'll explain.

283
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:24,009
We wanted to help you, so we paid a
visit to the town where you used to live.

284
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:26,000
How could you?

285
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,534
Why would you do that?

286
00:18:30,980 --> 00:18:31,900
Wait, Sinon.

287
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,772
They found someone who wants to meet you.

288
00:18:34,860 --> 00:18:37,797
I can't let you leave till you
hear what they have to say.

289
00:18:37,880 --> 00:18:39,680
It might hurt, and I'm sorry.

290
00:18:40,400 --> 00:18:43,988
But I can't stand by if there's
a chance what they say helps.

291
00:18:45,720 --> 00:18:47,057
Who is this person?

292
00:18:47,140 --> 00:18:48,846
What do they want to tell me?

293
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:11,960
Sari, do I know you?

294
00:19:13,760 --> 00:19:17,760
Sachi Osawa, you're
Shino Asada, aren't you?

295
00:19:18,180 --> 00:19:20,592
I'd like to introduce you to my daughter.

296
00:19:20,920 --> 00:19:22,200
Her name's Miss.

297
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,675
She's four years old.

298
00:19:25,120 --> 00:19:26,920
I don't know if you remember.

299
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,735
But I used to work at the post office.

300
00:19:38,980 --> 00:19:39,880
I'm sorry.

301
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:42,580
This is really hard.

302
00:19:42,940 --> 00:19:44,060
See, I…

303
00:19:45,140 --> 00:19:47,081
I should have done this ages ago.

304
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:49,344
I'm so sorry it took this long.

305
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:53,680
I never apologized or
thanked you for what you did.

306
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:03,599
I was pregnant with her the day that
man came in and tried to rob us.

307
00:20:04,260 --> 00:20:08,140
What you did, it wasn't
just my life you saved.

308
00:20:08,340 --> 00:20:10,811
You saved the life of my little girl, too.

309
00:20:11,560 --> 00:20:12,619
Thank you so much.

310
00:20:13,340 --> 00:20:16,180
If it weren't for you,
she wouldn't be here.

311
00:20:17,520 --> 00:20:19,960
I saved your daughter?

312
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:23,580
Xenon, time to let go.

313
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:28,497
You've been blaming yourself way too long,
Beating yourself up over what happened.

314
00:20:28,580 --> 00:20:31,286
I'm not saying you're
wrong to do that, but...

315
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:37,400
It's just, whatever guilt
you feel about what you did,

316
00:20:37,660 --> 00:20:40,778
you got a right to consider
the lives you saved, too.

317
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:45,960
You got the right to think about
those people and forgive yourself.

318
00:20:46,540 --> 00:20:47,370
That's it.

319
00:20:47,453 --> 00:20:49,361
That's what I wanted you to know.

320
00:21:10,320 --> 00:21:12,217
I made it for you.

321
00:21:12,300 --> 00:21:14,537
Thank you for saving Mommy!

322
00:21:14,620 --> 00:21:16,657
And for saving me!

323
00:21:16,740 --> 00:21:18,940
We love you.

324
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:29,000
Oh, my God.

325
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,337
I don't need

326
00:22:47,420 --> 00:22:53,320
one more time.

327
00:22:53,620 --> 00:22:57,540
I want to be stronger and stronger.

328
00:22:58,660 --> 00:23:00,900
I want to be in the dark.

329
00:23:35,400 --> 00:23:37,920
Next time, debriefing.
